build_result: FAILED on the x86_64 Fly builder — but NOT a code defect. The build
              got through ~770 of 777 derivations and died building `bloch-0.1.0`
              (our node/wallet Rust package) for aarch64: the qemu-user emulation
              of the aarch64 Rust toolchain crashes (107 emulation-crash signals
              in the log — qemu:/SIGILL/SIGSEGV; rustc-hash/rustc-hex retried many
              times). This is the WRONG BUILDER, exactly as the flake header warns
              ("the mobile image … is cross-built or built natively on an aarch64
              Linux host — never [emulated]"). The rest of the image (kernel, DTB,
              rootfs, all mobile-nixos pkgs) built fine; only the emulated Rust
              leg failed. NEXT: run the same `nix build` on a NATIVE aarch64 host
              (e.g. an AWS Graviton) — no emulation, the Rust build is native —
              which should produce the artifact; THEN attempt the QEMU boot.
              No artifact, no hash, no boot claimed here.
